GPL components the engine runs
------------------------------

This repository pins and fetches the following; it does not distribute them.

ComfyUI (comfyanonymous/ComfyUI): GPL-3.0.
  Cloned at a pinned commit into the refiner's own virtual environment. The
  two TRELLIS.2 worker files, backend/workers/trellis2_fp8_worker.py and
  backend/workers/trellis_refiner_worker.py, import ComfyUI modules in the
  same Python process. No ComfyUI server is started.
PyMeshLab (cnr-isti-vclab/PyMeshLab): GPL-3.0.
  Imported by the TRELLIS.2 worker and by ComfyUI-Trellis2, in that same
  environment.
pymeshfix (pyvista/pymeshfix): GPL-3.0; the PyPI classifier for its 0.18
  releases says AGPL-3.0.
  The optional "meshfix" extra. Only the Instant Meshes clean method imports
  it; the default voxel clean does not.
Blender: GPL-2.0-or-later source, distributed as GPL-3.0 binaries.
  Runs the engine's bpy scripts inside its own process:
  backend/workers/blender_worker.py, unirig_bind_worker.py,
  blender_obj_worker.py, tools/blender/*.py and several scripts/*.py. Those
  scripts are released under the MIT License, which is compatible with the
  GPL, as Blender's licence asks of published scripts.
bpy 4.2: GPL-3.0.
  Installed into UniRig's own environment by scripts/setup_unirig.sh. UniRig
  runs as a separate program.

MIT is GPL-compatible, so the engine's own code can stay MIT. Anyone who
distributes a combined runtime takes on the GPL's obligations for that
bundle, such as a container image holding the engine together with ComfyUI,
PyMeshLab and Blender: licence texts and the corresponding source. They must
also leave MeshLib out unless its authors allow the transfer.


Model weights
-------------

No model weights are in this repository. `aismith-engine weights install`
downloads each file at the revision, size and sha256 that
vendor/weights.lock.json pins.

  trellis2-4b-fp8                visualbruno/TRELLIS.2-4B-FP8, a repack of
                                 microsoft/TRELLIS.2-4B                 MIT
  trellis-image-large-ss-decoder microsoft/TRELLIS-image-large          MIT
  dinov3-vitl16                  facebook/dinov3-vitl16-pretrain-lvd1689m
                                 DINOv3 License: custom, gated, not OSI
  unirig-skeleton-ar256          VAST-AI/UniRig                         MIT
  birefnet-general,              rembg's release of ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet MIT
  birefnet-general-lite

DINOv3: before installing, accept the DINOv3 License on the model's Hugging
Face page with your own account, and set HF_TOKEN for that account. Among other
things, the licence governs redistribution, asks for acknowledgement in
research publications, and carries trade-control terms and a list of
prohibited uses. Boundless Games, LLC's own acceptance is recorded in
LICENSES/dinov3-acceptance.md. It covers Boundless Games, LLC only.

The training-data terms behind TRELLIS.2, UniRig and BiRefNet have not been
reviewed here.

Other models the studio app can use, none of them pinned or installed by this
repository:
  - The optional source-fidelity metrics (the "identity" extra) load
    openai/clip-vit-large-patch14, facebook/dinov2-base (Apache-2.0) and VGG
    weights through lpips (BSD-2-Clause) when present. Check each model card.
  - Image preparation calls a ComfyUI server you run, with FLUX.2 [klein] base
    4B, its VAE and the Qwen3 4B text encoder (Apache-2.0).
  - Motion generation uses NVIDIA Kimodo, installed by hand: code
    Apache-2.0, nvidia/Kimodo-SOMA-RP-v1.1 weights under the NVIDIA Open Model
    License, and Meta Llama 3 8B Instruct under the Meta Llama 3 Community
    License.


